ive (HHI 0.01 across 548 companies in the universe; the top four hold 9% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are roughly flat over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 16% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 67% and a beta of 0.80, it is more defensive than the market.","Trading is thin (about $53K a day), below the $1.0M liquidity floor flagged; building a position would move the price.","In past sell-offs it fell 23% in the 2020 crash and 38% in the 2022 bear market."],"val":["The stock trades 35% below its DCF fair value of $219, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 29%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $150 to $328 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Industrials peers: EV/EBITDA 0.4 vs 13.4 (sector median).","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 4.1% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 0.9% (vs the 8% bar).","The price implies 2.6% annual cash-flow growth, 7pp less than the model expects."],"prof":["ROIC of 9% earns above the cost of capital of 8.0%, but the 1pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have been steady (CV 0.04).","It runs a 34% gross margin and converts 5% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9 and cash conversion of 1.69x.","ROE of 8% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.8x equity multiplier)."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.2x net debt to EBITDA ($5.8B of cash against $6.9B of debt), with interest covered 10.6x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 3.5, in the safe zone)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 4.2% over 3 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 36% of profits supports about 3.4% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 4.2%, and institutions hold 57%.","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.4% (1.6% in dividends).","It has paid a dividend for 12 consecutive years."],"people":["With about 104,095 employees, each generates about $302K of revenue, 0.8x the Industrials median.","That works out to $15K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.2M (7x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":63,"head":"Watch: thinly traded ($53K a day).","pros":["Trades 35% below fair value of $219","Net debt/EBITDA 0.2x","Piotroski F-score 7/9","Altman Z in the safe zone","EV/EBITDA 0.4x vs sector 13.4x"],"cons":["Thinly traded ($53K a day)","Flag: thin EDGAR history (0y)"],"flags":[],"need":["its composite (29) is below 39"],"buy_below":186.18,"vc":{"base":219.04,"base_src":"dcf","bear":150.16,"bull":327.57,"alt_median":71.1,"n_alt":3,"gap":2.0806,"dispersion":0.2905,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 208% above the other models' median ($71.10)"]},"med":{"pe":24.0501,"ev_ebitda":13.39,"pfcf":22.9066,"pb":2.9489,"roic":0.0996,"gross_margin":0.2855,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0143}},"mc_quantiles":[114.39,134.09,150.16,161.57,172.87,179.59,188.13,197.25,204.11,212.21,221.44,231.61,239.35,250.45,257.04,269.91,284.78,301.91,327.57,363.73,445.54],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.712,"discount_rate":0.152,"terminal_growth":0.014,"exit_multiple":0.122},"ticker":"DKILF","date":"2026-11-13"}